I have a TypeScript utility that processes API responses and formats them for the frontend. I'm worried about type safety because I used `any` in several places, and there are some `as` type assertions on external data without validation. Could you review this code and identify all critical and high-severity issues? Also, please suggest fixes following TypeScript best practices.

```typescript
// fetchUser.ts
import { api } from '../api';

export async function fetchUser(id: string): Promise<any> {
  const response = await api.get(`/users/${id}`);
  return response.data as User;
}

// formatUser.ts
export function formatUser(user: any): FormattedUser {
  return {
    fullName: `${user.firstName} ${user.lastName}`,
    age: user.age ?? 0,
  };
}

// types.d.ts
interface User {
  id: string;
  firstName: string;
  lastName: string;
  age?: number;
}

interface FormattedUser {
  fullName: string;
  age: number;
}
```

The project uses TypeScript 5.x with `strict: true` in `tsconfig.json`. I'm also looking for any `any[]`, `Function` types, or missing return types elsewhere in the codebase. Please provide a full audit focusing on type safety bypasses, unsafe assertions, and generic patterns.

