## Detection Rules

### Critical: Unmaintainable Code
| Pattern | Issue | Severity |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Function > 50 lines | Hard to test and understand | CRITICAL |
| Cyclomatic complexity > 15 | Too many decision points | CRITICAL |
| Nesting depth > 4 | Pyramid of doom | CRITICAL |
| Duplicate code > 10 lines | Violates DRY | CRITICAL |
| Unused parameters | Dead code signal | HIGH |
| Mixed concerns in single function | Violates SRP | HIGH |
| Hardcoded magic strings/numbers | Maintainability hazard | HIGH |

```typescript
// BAD: Long, complex function
function processUserData(input: Record<string, unknown>): string {
  // ... 60 lines with multiple if/else, loops, callbacks
  let result = '';
  for (const key in input) {
    if (input.hasOwnProperty(key)) {
      const val = input[key];
      if (typeof val === 'string') {
        result += val.toUpperCase();
      } else if (Array.isArray(val)) {
        val.forEach((item, idx) => {
          if (idx === 0) {
            result += item;
          } else {
            result += ',' + item;
          }
        });
      } else {
        // ... many more branches
      }
    }
  }
  return result;
}

// GOOD: Decomposed into small, single-purpose functions
function joinValues(input: string[]): string {
  return input.join(',');
}

function processStringArray(input: unknown): string {
  if (Array.isArray(input)) {
    return joinValues(input.map(String));
  }
  return '';
}

function processUserData(input: Record<string, unknown>): string {
  return Object.values(input).map(processStringArray).join('');
}
```

### High: Naming and Structure
| Pattern | Issue | Severity |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Inconsistent naming (camelCase vs snake_case) | Confusing | HIGH |
| Vague variable names (`data`, `temp`, `result`) | Reduces readability | HIGH |
| Boolean prefix not `is`/`has`/`should` | Hard to infer purpose | HIGH |
| Function name does not describe action | Misleading | HIGH |
| Deeply nested ternaries | Hard to read | HIGH |
| Missing `@param` or `@returns` on exported functions | Poor documentation | MEDIUM |
| Inline magic numbers without comments | Future confusion | MEDIUM |
| Unused imports or variables | Clutter | MEDIUM |

```typescript
// BAD: Poor naming
function abc(x: number, y: number[]) {
  let z = y.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
  return x * z;
}

// GOOD: Descriptive naming
function calculateTotalPrice(unitPrice: number, quantities: number[]): number {
  const totalQuantity = quantities.reduce((sum, qty) => sum + qty, 0);
  return unitPrice * totalQuantity;
}

// BAD: Boolean without prefix
function valid(user: User): boolean {
  return user.age >= 18;
}
// GOOD: is prefix
function isValidUser(user: User): boolean {
  return user.age >= 18;
}
```

### Medium: Documentation and Comments
| Pattern | Issue | Severity |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Public API without JSDoc | Hinders consumers | MEDIUM |
| Outdated or misleading comments | Worse than no comment | MEDIUM |
| Comment describing *what* instead of *why* | Redundant with code | LOW |
| Missing `@throws` in JSDoc | Surprise to callers | MEDIUM |
| No inline comments for complex logic | Hard to follow | LOW |

```typescript
