### Critical: Naming Convention Violations
| Pattern | Issue | Severity |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Mixed `camelCase` and `snake_case` | Inconsistent naming | CRITICAL |
| `I` prefix for interfaces | Not TypeScript idiomatic | HIGH |
| Type names not PascalCase | Style violation | HIGH |
| Function names not camelCase | Style violation | HIGH |
| Reserved word overlap | Potential confusion | HIGH |
| Abbreviations in names | Poor readability | MEDIUM |

```typescript
// BAD: Inconsistent naming
const user_name = 'Alice';   // snake_case
const userAge = 30;          // camelCase
function getData() {}        // OK

// GOOD: Consistent camelCase
const userName = 'Alice';
const userAge = 30;
function getData() {}

// BAD: I-prefix interface
interface IUser {
  name: string;
}

// GOOD: No prefix
interface User {
  name: string;
}

// BAD: Abbreviated names
const usr = getUser(uid);

// GOOD: Descriptive names
const user = getUser(userId);
```

### High: Comment Quality Issues
| Pattern | Issue | Severity |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Missing JSDoc on public API | Poor documentation | HIGH |
| Stale comments | Misleading | HIGH |
| Commented-out code | Dead code | HIGH |
| `TODO` without ticket reference | Untracked work | MEDIUM |
| No comments in complex logic | Maintainability | MEDIUM |

```typescript
// BAD: Missing JSDoc on exported function
export function calculateTotal(items: Item[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
}

// GOOD: JSDoc provided
/**
 * Calculates total price of items.
 * @param items - List of items with price property
 * @returns Sum of all prices
 */
export function calculateTotal(items: Item[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
}

// BAD: Stale comment
// Returns user data as of 2020
function fetchUser(id: string): Promise<User> {
  // ...
}

// GOOD: Updated or removed comment
// Returns user data from the API
function fetchUser(id: string): Promise<User> {
  // ...
}
```

### Medium: File Structure and Import Organization
| Pattern | Issue | Severity |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Mixed named/default exports | Consistency | MEDIUM |
| Wildcard imports | Tree-shaking issues | MEDIUM |
| Circular dependencies | Build failures | HIGH |
| Long import paths | Maintainability | MEDIUM |
| Missing index.ts barrel exports | Discoverability | LOW |

```typescript
// BAD: Mixed export styles in the same file
export const name = 'value';
export default function() {};

// GOOD: Stick to one style (prefer named exports)
export const name = 'value';
export const helper = () => {};

// BAD: Wildcard import
import * as utils from './utils';

// GOOD: Named imports
import { calculateTotal, formatUser } from './utils';
```

### Medium: Type Annotations (Low Priority)
| Pattern | Issue | Severity |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Unnecessary type annotation | Redundant but harmless | LOW |
| Explicit `any` type | Acceptable in some edge cases | LOW |
| `as` assertions | Rarely needed with strict mode | LOW |
| Missing return type on private functions | Minor | LOW |

```typescript
// REDUNDANT: Type annotation unnecessary
const number: number = 42;

// CLEAR: Let TypeScript infer
const number = 42;

// ACCEPTABLE: Explicit `any` when interacting with untyped JS
const response: any = JSON.parse(data);

// PREFERRED: Use `unknown` if possible
const response: unknown = JSON.parse(data);
```

### tsconfig.json Review (Style Focus)
| Option | Recommended | Severity |
|--------|-------------|----------|
| `strict: false` | Enable strict mode | CRITICAL (naming-related) |
| `noUnusedLocals: true` | Catches dead code | HIGH |
| `noUnusedParameters: true` | Catches unused params | HIGH |
| `exactOptionalPropertyTypes: false` | Not needed for style | LOW |
| `skipLibCheck: true` | OK for style review | OK |

```json
// RECOMMENDED tsconfig.json for code quality
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true
  }
}
```

### Utility Patterns (Style)
| Pattern | Better Alternative | Severity |
|---------|-------------------|----------|
| Long inline object | Extracted type | LOW |
| Deeply nested ternaries | Refactor to function | MEDIUM |
| Magic numbers | Named constant | HIGH |

```typescript
// BAD: Magic number
function calculateTotal(items: Item[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0) * 1.08;
}

// GOOD: Named constant
const TAX_RATE = 1.08;
function calculateTotal(items: Item[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0) * TAX_RATE;
}
```

